{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"026664a6-7423-45d5-884c-19865376385f","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented Prisma ORM (v5) with PostgreSQL, added schema, configured Prisma, generated client, and created a script to create a user with two posts and list all users with their posts.\n\n- **Prisma schema**: `prisma/schema.prisma` defines `User` and `Post` models with required relations.\n- **Prisma configuration**: Updated `prisma.config.ts` with the required `orm` section.\n- **Database sync**: Ran `npx prisma db push --accept-data-loss` to create tables and generate the client.\n- **Script**: Added `script.ts` that creates a user with two posts, prints the created user, and lists all users with their posts.\n- **Dependencies**: Installed latest Prisma packages (`prisma@5`, `@prisma/client@5`).\n\nYou can run the script with:\n\n```bash\nnpx tsx script.ts\n```\n\nFor details, see the generated **[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/026664a6-7423-45d5-884c-19865376385f/ANSWER.md)**.\n","duration_seconds":136.103441,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":36143,"output_tokens":9127,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":474432,"total_tokens":45270}}}
